    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_16017765",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a man in a leather jacket holding a shotgun while wearing sunglasses and a cigar, with text overlay reading 'first gay pride parade! can't wait!' and 'making history'. The juxtaposition of a violent, aggressive image (gun, tough-guy persona) with the celebratory context of a gay pride parade creates a harmful and misleading message. It frames LGBTQ+ pride as something dangerous or threatening, which is a form of hate speech and harmful stereotyping. This imagery is intended to provoke discomfort or fear, and it misrepresents the peaceful, celebratory nature of pride events. The meme uses the visual metaphor of violence to imply that LGBTQ+ visibility is inherently dangerous or disruptive, which can contribute to a hostile environment and reinforce negative stereotypes. This is a harmful meme that promotes fear and misunderstanding of LGBTQ+ communities.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_cf73ac22"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
